"explanation": "Household electrical outlets are wired in parallel. This configuration ensures that each appliance receives the full supply voltage independently. Consequently, the operation (turning on or off) of one appliance does not alter the voltage or current available to the others, allowing them to function normally regardless of the state of the other devices. If they were connected in series, turning off one would break the circuit for all, and the voltage would be divided, preventing proper operation.",
